From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 08:40:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] configs: vendor: lge: enable the in-kernel low memory killer
 for Android 17's lmkd

Android 17's lmkd only knows two memory-pressure sources: PSI, or the
in-kernel lowmemorykiller module. The vmpressure/memcg fallback that
older lmkd used on 4.4 kernels is gone, and cgroups.json now puts the
memory controller in cgroup2, so lmkd dies on startup:

  lowmemorykiller: Old kill strategy can only be used with v1 cgroup hierarchy
  lowmemorykiller: Failed to initialize PSI monitors
  lowmemorykiller: exiting

init restarts it forever and /dev/socket/lmkd never appears. Every
ProcessList.writeLmkd() in system_server then blocks 3 s waiting for the
socket while holding the AMS lock, which ANRs systemui, phone, nfc and
the network stack; the network stack death becomes
"IllegalStateException: Lost network stack" and system_server is killed
every ~80 s.

This kernel has no PSI (no kernel/sched/psi.c), but it does ship
drivers/staging/android/lowmemorykiller.c. With the module built in,
lmkd finds /sys/module/lowmemorykiller/parameters/minfree, switches to
its in-kernel interface and never touches PSI or memcg.
---
 arch/arm64/configs/vendor/lge/lge_msm8996_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/lge/lge_msm8996_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/lge/lge_msm8996_defconfig
index 6e1fe9f6240a..3d29d4a9a0d7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/lge/lge_msm8996_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/vendor/lge/lge_msm8996_defconfig
@@ -844,7 +844,7 @@ CONFIG_SLIMBUS=y
 CONFIG_MFD_H1_DSV=y
 CONFIG_WQ_POWER_EFFICIENT_DEFAULT=y
 # CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_TIMES is not set
-# CONFIG_ANDROID_LOW_MEMORY_KILLER is not set
+CONFIG_ANDROID_LOW_MEMORY_KILLER=y
 # CONFIG_ESOC is not set
 CONFIG_BONDING=y
 # CONFIG_MSM_MHI is not set
